{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--affiliative-indexes-possessor-via-a-series","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"The affiliative form of a noun indexes the person and number of the possessor via the A-series (transitive-subject) cross-reference prefixes.","ja":"名詞の所属形には、A（他動詞主語）系列の相互参照接頭辞によって所有者の人称・数が標示される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest","doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku=","ci=","e=","eci=","a="],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2014@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-08","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0009-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2022pos@handbook-epub/l0093-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--affiliative-form-possessor-optional-np","differs_in":null,"note":"Internal indexing of possessor makes overt NP optional"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking-diachronic-expansion","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"Because using genitive pronouns is mechanically simpler than forming concrete forms for each noun, the genitive construction expanded and led to double marking such as akor amachihi ('my wife').","ja":"領格代名詞を用いる表現は機械的で労力が少なくて済むため歓迎されて領域を拡大し、最終的にはakor amachihiのような二重標示表現を生むに至った。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:scope unstated"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["akor amachihi","ekor emachihi","kor machihi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0040-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--akor-machihi-analogical-error","differs_in":null,"note":"The analogical error claim is a more specific evaluative consequence of the diachronic expansion"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--akor-machihi-analogical-error","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"By analogy from kor mat = kor machihi, forms such as akor machihi or ekor machihi have begun to appear even among Ainu speakers, though traditional elders strictly avoid this.","ja":"kor mat = kor machihi からの類推により、akor machihi や ekor machihi のような誤った表現がアイヌ自身の間でも用いられそうになっているが、古格を守る古老の言語では絶対に生じない。"},"type":"judgement","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:scope unstated"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["akor machihi","ekor machihi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0041-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--intervening-elements-possessor-possessum","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu possessive constructions with an overt possessor NP and an affiliative noun, other syntactic elements such as particles can intervene between the possessor NP and the possessed noun.","ja":"アイヌ語の「名詞句＋名詞所属形」の表現では、所有者名詞句と被所有名詞の間に助詞などの要素が介在して分断されることがごく普通に起きる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0173-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--weak-bond-pronoun-personal-form","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, expressions consisting of a (pro)noun plus a personal form of a noun do not strictly form a single tight noun phrase corresponding to Japanese 'A no B', but rather have a weak bond between A and B.","ja":"アイヌ語の「(代)名詞＋人称形」は、厳密には「AのB」というひとまとまりの句をなしているわけではなく、AとBの結びつきは弱い。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0174-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--possessor-precedes-possessed-affiliative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--double-marking"],"statement":{"en":"The nominal possessive expression takes the form of the possessor noun followed by the possessive (affiliative) form of the possessed noun.","ja":"名詞の所有表現は、所有者名詞に被所有名詞の所有形（所属形）が後続する形をとる。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0027-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--alienable-possessor-as-verbal-argument","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu possessive marking of alienables, the possessor is coded not as a dependent in an NP but as an argument in a finite clause, and the appositive word is a verb.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡可能所有標示において、所有者は名詞句内の従属部としてではなく定形節の項としてコード化され、同格語は動詞である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0001-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-relative-clause-alienable-possession","differs_in":null,"note":"Both characterize the kor construction as verbal/clausal rather than nominal"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--earlier-ainu-multiple-alienable-classes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"When Ainu was still the daily language of a large speech community, it had multiple alienable class constructions.","ja":"かつてアイヌ語が大規模な言語共同体の日常言語であった際、複数の譲渡可能名詞クラス構文を有していた。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"proposed","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0001-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--classifiers-shrunk-to-one-modern","differs_in":null,"note":"Earlier multiple classes → modern single classifier"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-verbal-appositive-classifier-system","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu has an appositive classifier system that uses verbs.","ja":"アイヌ語には動詞を用いる同格分類詞体系が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0037-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-relative-clause-alienable-possession","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"Alienable nouns in Ainu use a relative construction with 'have' (kor) in which the possessor is marked as the subject of kor and the possessed noun is the gapped object of kor.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡可能名詞は「持つ」（kor）を用いた関係節構文を使用し、所有者が「持つ」の主語として標示され、被所有名詞は「持つ」の空所化された目的語となる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--alienable-person-markers-verbal","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The person markers used in the Ainu alienable possessive construction are unambiguously verbal person markers.","ja":"アイヌ語の譲渡可能所有構文で用いられる人称標識は、明白に動詞の人称標識である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--appositive-verb-is-finite","differs_in":null,"note":"Verbal person markers imply the appositive is a finite verb form"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--appositive-verb-is-finite","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"In Ainu, the appositive verb modifying a possessed noun is finite.","ja":"アイヌ語において、被所有名詞を修飾する同格動詞は定形である。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0006-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-human-nouns-affective-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The kor construction with human nouns and human attributes is used with high frequency partly due to an extended affective function expressing affection.","ja":"人間名詞や人間の属性を表す名詞においてkor構文の頻度が高いのは、愛情を表す派生的な用法の存在が一因と考えられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"asserted","conditions":["human nouns"]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--transitive-verbs-as-possessive-classifiers-oral-lit","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"In oral literature, a number of transitive verbs other than kor functioned as possessive classifiers specifying the type of possessive relation in prenominal relative clauses.","ja":"口承文芸において、kor以外のいくつかの他動詞が前置名詞修飾関係節において所有関係の種類を指定・分類する所有分類詞としての機能を果たしていた。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"asserted","conditions":["oral literature"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--larger-classifier-system-reconstructible","differs_in":null,"note":"Oral literature evidence supports reconstruction of larger classifier system"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--un-classificatory-possessive-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb un 'attach to, belong' functions as a classificatory possessive verb in expressions like a-un cise 'my house'.","ja":"動詞un「〜につく、〜に属する」は、a-un cise「私の家」のような表現において分類的所持動詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["un"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0013-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--mut-classificatory-possessive-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb mut 'wear (a sword)' functions as a classificatory possessive verb in expressions like a-mut emusi 'my sword'.","ja":"動詞mut「（刀を）帯びる」は、a-mut emusi「私の刀」のような表現において分類的所持動詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["mut"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0014-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ante-classificatory-possessive-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb ante (causative of an 'exist') functions as a classificatory possessive verb meaning 'husband' in e-an-te hoku 'your husband'.","ja":"動詞ante（an「存在する」の使役形）は、e-an-te hoku「あなたの夫」において「夫」を表す分類的所持動詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["an-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0014-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--hekote-classificatory-possessive-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb hekote 'be married to' functions as a classificatory possessive verb with spouse and family terms.","ja":"動詞hekote「〜と結婚している」は、配偶者や親族の語とともに分類的所持動詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["hekote"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0014-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--mi-classificatory-possessive-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb mi 'wear' functions as a classificatory possessive verb in expressions like a-mi kosonde 'my kimono'.","ja":"動詞mi「着る」は、a-mi kosonde「私の着物」のような表現において分類的所持動詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["mi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0014-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
