{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-takes-adverbial-modifiers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The possessive relative clause predicate kor 'have' can take adverbial modifiers.","ja":"所有関係節述語 kor「持つ」は副詞的修飾語を伴うことができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0015-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-third-person-zero-phonological-unit","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"When the possessor is third person, kor 'have' lacks overt person marking and tends to form a single phonological unit with the following possessum head noun, preceded by a pause after the possessor NP.","ja":"所有者が3人称の場合、kor「持つ」は明示的な人称標示を欠き、所有者名詞句の後に休止を伴って後続の被所有主要部名詞と単一の音調単位を形成する傾向がある。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":["third-person possessor"]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0016-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-one-classifier-verbal-appositive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu has a one-classifier verbal appositive possessive system.","ja":"アイヌ語は分類詞を1つだけ持つ動詞同格所有体系を有する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0018-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--sole-classifier-is-verb","differs_in":null,"note":"Sole-classifier-is-verb specifies the membership of the one-classifier system"},{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--verbal-appositives-one-or-two-verbs","differs_in":"scope","note":"One claim says exactly one classifier; the other says one or two verbs"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--sole-classifier-is-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The sole classifier of Ainu is a verb.","ja":"アイヌ語における唯一の分類詞は動詞である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0021-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--verbal-appositives-one-or-two-verbs","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verbal appositives in Ainu form a small system of one or two verbs, usually meaning 'own' or 'have'.","ja":"アイヌ語における動詞同格語は、「所有する」または「持つ」を意味する1つまたは2つの動詞からなる小さな体系である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0024-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--older-ainu-larger-classifier-subdivisions","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"In older Ainu, larger appositive classifier systems add subdivisions of food by preparation type, clothing, instruments and objects by function, fire and fire-related things, houses, various items by history of acquisition, and others.","ja":"より古い時代のアイヌ語における大規模な同格的所有分類詞体系では、調理形態による食物の細分化、衣服、機能による道具や物品、火および火に関連する事物、家屋、獲得の経緯による様々な品目などが付け加わる。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"asserted","conditions":["older Ainu"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0031-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--classifiers-shrunk-to-one-modern","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The several possessive classifiers of earlier Ainu have shrunk to just one in the modern variety.","ja":"より古い段階のアイヌ語に存在した複数の所属類別詞は、現代の変種においてはただ1つにまで減少している。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0032-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-one-classifier-verbal-appositive","differs_in":null,"note":"Diachronic reduction explains the synchronic one-classifier state"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--larger-classifier-system-reconstructible","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"A larger verbal classifier system is reconstructible for earlier Ainu, in which classifiers relate to the history and cultural status of possession.","ja":"初期のアイヌ語には、分類詞が所有の歴史や文化的地位に関与する、より大規模な動詞的分類詞体系が再構可能である。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"proposed","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0037-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--older-ainu-larger-classifier-subdivisions","differs_in":null,"note":"Older-ainu-larger-classifier-subdivisions gives the specific semantic categories of the reconstructed system"},{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--earlier-ainu-multiple-alienable-classes","differs_in":null,"note":"Both assert a richer earlier system"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-genitive-only-with-personhood","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The particle/verb kor can only be used to express possession when the possessor has personhood.","ja":"所属されるものが人格を有するときに限り、kor をもって属格を表すことができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:scope unstated"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":["possessor has personhood"]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0040-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0047-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0154-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0027-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-human-nouns-affective-frequency","differs_in":null,"note":"Restriction to human/personhood domain explains high frequency with human nouns"},{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-relative-clause-alienable-possession","differs_in":"scope","note":"Kindaichi & Chiri restrict kor to human possessors; Bugaeva's analysis covers alienables more broadly"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--shizunai-most-possession-via-kor","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"Most expressions of possession in Shizunai Ainu are constructed with the attributive postposition kor.","ja":"静内アイヌ語における所有表現の大半は、連体格後置詞 kor を用いて構成される。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0080-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--three-possessive-construction-types","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Shizunai shows kor-dominant pattern; general Ainu description posits three construction types"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-between-nouns-attributive-postposition","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"When the verb kor 'have' is placed directly between two nouns or between a pronominal affix and a noun representing possessor and possessed respectively, it functions as an attributive postposition.","ja":"動詞 kor「持つ」が、それぞれ所有者と被所有者を表す2つの名詞の間、あるいは人称接辞と名詞の間に直接置かれるとき、連体助詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0154-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-marker-of-possession-chitose","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Shizunai description specifies structural position; Chitose description is more general"},{"kind":"contradicts","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--alienable-possessor-as-verbal-argument","differs_in":"framework","note":"Refsing analyzes kor as a postposition; Bugaeva analyzes it as a finite verb with the possessor as its argument"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-marker-of-possession-chitose","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The verb kor 'to have' is also used as a marker expressing possession ('of') in Chitose Ainu.","ja":"動詞 kor「持つ」は、「〜の」という所有を表す形式としても用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0117-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-personal-affix-genitive-pronouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-appositive"],"statement":{"en":"The genitive relation of personal pronouns can be expressed by the verb kor 'to have' with an appropriate personal affix followed by the possessed noun.","ja":"人称代名詞の属格関係は、適切な人称接辞を伴う動詞 kor「持つ」に被所有名詞が後続する形によって表されうる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0027-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-relative-clause-alienable-possession","differs_in":"framework","note":"Shibatani describes the same construction without the relative-clause analysis"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--inalienable-alienable-combine-nested","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--nested"],"statement":{"en":"Inalienable and alienable possessive constructions can combine into larger syntactic structures.","ja":"譲渡不能所有構文と譲渡可能所有構文は組み合わさってより大きな統語構造を形成することができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"existential","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0016-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-lacks-genitive-case","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu lacks genitive case marking for expressing possession.","ja":"アイヌ語には所有を表す属格格標示が存在しない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0016-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0027-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-possession-typologically-typical","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Possessive constructions in Ainu are typologically typical and are fully accounted for by the cross-linguistic framework of nominal argument structure, valence, and appositive possession.","ja":"アイヌ語の所有構文は極めて典型的であり、名詞の項構造・結合価と同格所有に関する通言語的枠組みによって十全に説明される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0039-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--ainu-remnant-north-asian-appositive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu can be interpreted as a remnant of an earlier, larger group of North Asian Circum-Pacific languages with appositive possession, the others having been absorbed by expansions of Tungusic, Japonic, Korean, Sinitic, and Austronesian.","ja":"アイヌ語は、同格所有を有していた北アジア環太平洋諸言語のかつて存在したより大きな集団の残存として解釈でき、他の言語群はツングース系、日琉系、朝鮮系、中国系、オーストロネシア系の拡大に吸収された。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"proposed","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0039-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--three-possessive-construction-types","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Possessive expressions corresponding to Japanese 'Noun1 no Noun2' take three types of constructions in Ainu: (1) N1 kor N2 (concept), (2) N1 N2 (affiliative), and (3) N1 (concept) N2 (concept).","ja":"日本語で「名詞₁の名詞₂」と訳されるアイヌ語の所有表現には、(1) 名詞₁ kor 名詞₂（概念形）、(2) 名詞₁ 名詞₂（所属形）、(3) 名詞₁（概念形）名詞₂（概念形）の3通りの構文がある。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0214-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--kor-relative-clause-alienable-possession","differs_in":null,"note":"Construction type (1) corresponds to the kor relative clause construction"},{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--possessor-precedes-possessed-affiliative","differs_in":null,"note":"Construction type (2) corresponds to the affiliative ordering construction"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--constructions-1-2-allow-prefix-not-3","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In possessive constructions (1) and (2), Noun1 can be replaced by a transitive subject personal prefix, whereas in the juxtaposition construction (3) it cannot.","ja":"所有構文(1)と(2)の名詞₁は他動詞の主格人称接辞に置き換えることができるが、(3)の構文では置き換えることができない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["ku="],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0215-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--genitive-precedes-head-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--overview"],"statement":{"en":"A genitive precedes the head noun in Ainu.","ja":"アイヌ語において属格名詞は主要部名詞に先行する。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-13","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--possessor-precedes-possessed-affiliative","differs_in":null,"note":"Both assert possessor-before-possessed ordering"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--third-person-possessor-prefix-zero","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--personal-prefixes"],"statement":{"en":"The third-person possessor prefix is zero, so a possessed noun form standing alone by default means 'his/her/its ...'.","ja":"三人称所有者接頭辞はゼロであるため、所有接尾辞形の名詞が単独で立つ場合のデフォルトの解釈は「彼／彼女／それの…」となる。"},"type":"paradigm-cell","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["Ø-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2021poss@pdftotext-pieces/l0010-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--affiliative-form-possessor-optional-np","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topics":["topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking","topic:nominal/adnominal-possession-double-marking--personal-prefixes"],"statement":{"en":"A noun in its affiliative person form indexes the possessor internally and can stand alone to express a possessed meaning, so an independent possessor noun phrase is grammatically optional.","ja":"名詞の人称形は人称接辞によって名詞内部に所有者の人称が表示されているため単独で完結した所属の意味を表すことができ、対応する所有者名詞句は文法的に必須ではない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"categorical","conditions":[]},"forms":["siki"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0173-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T08-28-07-458Z","status":"grouped"}
